From: corruptmods <13516012+corruptmods@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] videotoolbox: Dolby Vision profile 7 mode as a decoder AVOption

Patch 0003 read getenv("PLEZY_DV_CONVERSION_MODE") inside libavcodec on
every slice and every session-format query: a process-global setting with
no API, read on the decode path.

The HEVC decoder gets a private AVOption, dv_conversion_mode
(unset|auto|disabled|dv81|hevc_strip, default unset). ff_videotoolbox_
common_init() resolves it once into the hwaccel context; with the option
unset it reads the environment once there instead, PLUET_DV_CONVERSION_MODE
before PLEZY_DV_CONVERSION_MODE, with the same values and aliases as
before, so embedders that set the variable keep working. With neither set
the mode is auto, as before. The helpers that read the mode take the codec
context instead of calling getenv().

Every VideoToolbox hwaccel shares that init, and VP9's and ProRes's
priv_data do not start with an AVClass, so the option is only looked up for
HEVC, and through the codec context with AV_OPT_SEARCH_CHILDREN, which
descends into priv_data only when the codec has a priv_class. Other codecs
resolve to auto without reading the environment.

scripts/test_vt_dovi_conversion_mode.sh compiles the resolution code and
the option's table lines against stub FFmpeg types, then runs the resolution
against a real minimal libavcodec with opened HEVC, H.264, VP9 and ProRes
decoders, the last two with a wild first pointer in priv_data, which a
lookup on priv_data dereferences.


diff --git a/libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.c b/libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.c
index e916a1a..651401b 100644
--- a/libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.c
+++ b/libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.c
@@ -4225,6 +4225,18 @@ static const AVOption options[] = {
         { "unspecified", .type = AV_OPT_TYPE_CONST, .default_val = { .i64 = AV_STEREO3D_VIEW_UNSPEC }, .unit = "view_pos" },
         { "left",        .type = AV_OPT_TYPE_CONST, .default_val = { .i64 = AV_STEREO3D_VIEW_LEFT },   .unit = "view_pos" },
         { "right",       .type = AV_OPT_TYPE_CONST, .default_val = { .i64 = AV_STEREO3D_VIEW_RIGHT },  .unit = "view_pos" },
+    { "dv_conversion_mode", "Dolby Vision profile 7 handling under VideoToolbox",
+        OFFSET(dv_conversion_mode), AV_OPT_TYPE_INT, { .i64 = -1 }, -1, 3, PAR, .unit = "dv_conversion_mode" },
+        { "unset",      "PLUET_DV_CONVERSION_MODE or PLEZY_DV_CONVERSION_MODE, else auto",
+                        0, AV_OPT_TYPE_CONST, { .i64 = -1 }, 0, 0, PAR, .unit = "dv_conversion_mode" },
+        { "auto",       "convert to profile 8.1 where libdovi is linked",
+                        0, AV_OPT_TYPE_CONST, { .i64 = 0 },  0, 0, PAR, .unit = "dv_conversion_mode" },
+        { "disabled",   "hand profile 7 to VideoToolbox as it is",
+                        0, AV_OPT_TYPE_CONST, { .i64 = 1 },  0, 0, PAR, .unit = "dv_conversion_mode" },
+        { "dv81",       "convert to profile 8.1",
+                        0, AV_OPT_TYPE_CONST, { .i64 = 2 },  0, 0, PAR, .unit = "dv_conversion_mode" },
+        { "hevc_strip", "drop the RPUs and decode the base layer as HEVC",
+                        0, AV_OPT_TYPE_CONST, { .i64 = 3 },  0, 0, PAR, .unit = "dv_conversion_mode" },
 
     { NULL },
 };
diff --git a/libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.h b/libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.h
index 911d5c3..6a327d7 100644
--- a/libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.h
+++ b/libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.h
@@ -564,6 +564,10 @@ typedef struct HEVCContext {
                             ///< as a format defined in 14496-15
     int apply_defdispwin;
 
+    // Dolby Vision profile 7 handling under VideoToolbox (dv_conversion_mode);
+    // -1 leaves it to the environment, read once at hwaccel init.
